    13	
    14	## Analytic / Explicit Formula / Zeta Zeros
    15	
    16	| Approach | Verdict | Mode | Key Finding | Session |
    17	|----------|---------|------|-------------|---------|
    18	| Sparse matrix model for zeta zeros | FAIL | I | Tridiagonal Jacobi fits zeros with <0.05% error but uses 2N-1 params for N zeros (no compression). Off-diagonal entries b_i have 35% variation, no simple pattern. Toeplitz (N params) degrades at N=100. True extrapolation: 0.8-2.6% error. Information content not reduced. | 25 |
    19	| Zeta-zero structure persists at N=2000 (S25 caveat resolved) | FAIL | I | Extension of S25 tests to N=2000. Pair-correlation RMS deviation from GUE *shrinks* from ~0.10 to 0.0864. PSLQ on never-tested LATE block γ_{1001..1100}: 0/1225 pairs, 0/4060 triples. Cross-block (early × late) PSLQ: 0/400. Discrepancy/Weyl ratios match N=1000. No structure emerges at 2x scale. See `experiments/analytic/zeta_structure/zeta_structure_n2000_results.md`. | 45 |
    20	| Explicit formula partial sums recurrence | FAIL | I | No linear (r<=20), nonlinear (deg<=3), or difference recurrence. Residuals 2-6%. GUE phases make each term unpredictable from predecessors | 25 |
    21	| Zeta zero pairwise rational relations | FAIL | I | 499,500 ratios tested; closest to p/q (q<=100) matches are no better than random (KS p=1.3e-6 but wrong direction — zeros FARTHER from rationals). GUE repulsion effect. | 25 |
    22	| PSLQ linear relations among zeros | FAIL | I | 13,000+ tests at 60-digit precision: zero relations among subsets of 3-5 zeros with {1,pi,log(2pi)}. 1,225 pairwise tests negative. Large-K hits are lattice artifacts (random baseline confirms). Zeros linearly independent over Q. | 25 |
    23	| DFT spectral structure of zeros | FAIL | I | Power spectrum matches GUE (corr=0.9999). Spectral flatness 0.93-0.999 at high freq (white noise). Pair correlation matches GUE 1-(sin(pi*r)/(pi*r))^2. Only faint p=2 signal (12x median). Number variance logarithmic (GUE). O(N) bits incompressible. | 25 |
    24	| Zeta zeros mod constants (equidistribution) | FAIL | I | gamma_n mod m uniform for all 10 moduli tested (1, pi, log(2pi), 2pi, e, log(2,3,5,7)). KS p-values all >0.4. Weyl sums at 1/sqrt(N). Discrepancy BELOW random (GUE repulsion). Joint (mod 1, mod pi) independent. No arithmetic structure. | 25 |
    25	| Convergence acceleration of zero sum | FAIL | I | Tested Richardson, Aitken Δ², Shanks, Padé, Cesàro, Euler-Maclaurin on partial zero sums for x=10^4..10^7. Errors GROW as N^{+1.0} (random walk). Best method (Shanks) gives O(1) improvement only. GUE-random phases make each term independent — no structured error to accelerate. | 32 |
    26	| Self-correcting explicit formula + integer constraints | FAIL | I | Use fewer zeros + rounding/monotonicity/primality constraints. Truncation error is systematic bias ~O(N), not random noise. Constraints only help when error < 1, but error >> 1 with few zeros. Autocorr > 0.98. No triangulation possible. | 35,36 |
    27	| Explicit formula proper convergence (mpmath R(x^ρ)) | FAIL | I | Naive R(x^ρ) summation DIVERGES: error grows from 3.5 (K=0) to 2076 (K=100) at x=10^4. Complex li branch cuts cause numerical instability. Only Lagarias-Odlyzko contour method is numerically stable. | 36 |
    28	| Explicit formula + few zeros | FAIL | E | K^{-0.01} convergence | 5 |
    29	| Explicit formula + 50 zeros | FAIL | I | More zeros can make WORSE | 6 |
    30	| Explicit formula + 30 zeros | PARTIAL | E | 10% exact, best analytic | 10 |
