    5	## What Was Tested
    6	
    7	Seven modular-forms-based experiments: (1) Ramanujan tau function prime detection via tau(n) mod m, (2) j-invariant / moonshine coefficients, (3) Hecke eigenvalues encoding primes, (4) eta product prime indicators, (5) half-integral weight forms / theta series, (6) overconvergent modular forms / p-adic interpolation, (7) mock modular forms / Ramanujan mock theta coefficients vs primes.
    8	
    9	## Key Findings
    10	
    11	- tau(n) mod m: congruences hold but require knowing which n are prime (circular)
    12	- j-invariant: only 9 Heegner numbers, a finite and insufficient resource
    13	- Hecke eigenvalues: multiplicativity means detecting primes via eigenvalues IS factoring
    14	- Eta products: no prime indicator pattern found beyond trivial divisibility
    15	- Half-integral weight / theta series: encode representation counts, not primes directly
    16	- Overconvergent forms: p-adic interpolation does not bypass the summation barrier
    17	- Mock modular forms: coefficient patterns are statistical, not exact
    18	
    19	## Verdict
