    The search results primarily document historical milestones:
    
    - The Odlyzko–Schönhage algorithm is a fast algorithm for evaluating the Riemann zeta function at many points, introduced by Odlyzko and Schönhage in 1988.
    
    - The latest RH verification on the first 10^13 zeros was achieved using the fast Zeta multi-evaluation algorithm by Odlyzko and Schönhage, and was the first RH verification done with this technique.
    
    - In 2004, Gourdon presented an optimization of the Odlyzko–Schoenhage algorithm that efficiently computes the Riemann zeta function at large heights and facilitates the computation of zeros, enabling computation of two billion zeros from the 10^24-th zero.
    
    - More recently, in 2021, Platt and Trudgian verified that the Riemann Hypothesis is true up to a very large height in a rigorous way using interval arithmetic.
    
