    ## Title and Content
    
    The paper is titled "Nontrivial Riemann Zeros as Spectrum" by Enderalp Yakaboylu. 
    
    The paper addresses the Hilbert-Pólya Conjecture (HPC). It introduces a non-symmetric operator R on L²([0,∞)) with spectrum related to the zeros of the Riemann zeta function.
    
    The work shows that assuming the simplicity of all nontrivial Riemann zeros, a compression of R is intertwined with its adjoint by a positive semidefinite operator W, with the positivity of W enforcing that all nontrivial Riemann zeros have real part equal to 1/2, in accordance with the Riemann Hypothesis.
    
    The paper has gone through multiple revisions with the latest version being v15 as of March 11, 2026.
    
    
