    Based on the search results, I found a highly relevant arxiv paper matching your query:
    
    ## Key Finding
    
    The paper "On the exponents of distribution of primes and smooth numbers" by Alexandru Pascadi shows that both primes and smooth numbers are equidistributed in arithmetic progressions to moduli up to x^(5/8−o(1)), using triply-well-factorable weights for the primes (with improvements for the well-factorable linear sieve weights).
    
    This completely eliminates the dependency on Selberg's eigenvalue conjecture in previous works of Lichtman and the author, which built in turn on results of Maynard and Drappeau.
    
    ## Methodological Approach
    
    The work relies on recent large sieve inequalities for exceptional Maass forms of the author for additively-structured sequences, and on a related result of Watt for multiplicatively-structured sequences.
    
    ## Applications
    
    As applications, the paper proves refined upper bounds for the counts of twin primes and consecutive smooth numbers up to x.
    
    The paper is arxiv 2505.00653 and was posted in June 2025.
    
    
