    1	# Session 49 Proposals (2026-04-26)
    2	
    3	Three concrete proposals attacking p(n) in O(polylog). Each has a small-n
    4	test script in `experiments/proposals/session49_*.py`.
    5	
    6	The high-level frame: p(n) = R^{-1}(n) + delta(n) where delta carries the
    7	"oscillatory" content. Every proposal asks: is delta secretly compressible
    8	in a way that orthodox truncation of the explicit formula does not see?
    9	
    10	---
